.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:38:56-08:00","id":824254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824222-how-do-lunes-look?p=824244#post824244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm not going to get buy the 1st ed books just for Lune Descriptions, so I'll have to do with what's in second edition and forums. Anyways, thanks for responses. That picture is especially interesting, nofather.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I could take the credit.<br /> <br /> Depending on your interest, it could be a good get. The Predators book has descriptions and stat-blocks for 61 different spirits, including the lunes and helions, as well as building blocks for the primary hosts, azlu and beshilu, with write ups for various types of them, as well as write-ups for one each of the locust, crow and snake hosts. And the chapter on urged and claimed really has a lot of information about those, and descriptions and stat-blocks for pre-made urged, ridden and claimed. It's a pretty good resource for Werewolf, especially since you can get it cheap on Amazon but obviously if all you want is lune descriptions it's an easy choice to avoid.<br /> <br /> The reason I mention is because while spirits have changed how they interact with the different worlds in the shift to 