e wonder for months now and periodically pester Chris who would like to say something, but can't and points for months now that &quot;next week Stew might/should give you more info on The Pack&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Upcoming Projects page seems to be way out of date. It was on the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/153331/Onyx-Path-20152016-Publishing-Brochure\" target=\"_blank\">2015-2016 publishing brochure from GenCon.</a><br /> <br /> 'One part family, one part gang, and one part military unit, a werewolf\u2019s pack ties her to other werewolves, Wolf-Blooded, and a wide network of humans that ground her in the mundane world. This book is a thorough look at the pack from within and without.'<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I want spoilers too, but I appreciate that it's not up to Acrozatarim and Bunyip, and while Stew has posted here, he doesn't seem to do it often so I figure he doesn't usually check the forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T04:28:20-08:00","id":825356,"title":"","content":"*makes spooky foreshadowing noises*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T06:00:22-08:00","id":825370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824222-how-do-lunes-look?p=825356#post825356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*makes spooky foreshadowing noises*</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That's all you got? <br /> <br /> You should up your special effects budget there, buddy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T21:42:34-08:00","id":825759,"title":"","content":"I always imagine the Lunes to look like essentially blue-white skinned women with some crazy features like eyes shaped according to a specific lunar phase and such. But maybe I'm making my spirits look a bit to &quot;normal&quot; and it would be nice with more official pictures of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:11:45-08:00","id":825926,"title":"","content":"As servants of a god of shapeshifters, and spirits, they can generally choose any form to appear in they want.<br /> <br /> 'All Lunes have the ability to change their shape to some extent. Depending on their choir and the current phase of the moon, they may appear as abstracted beasts or humans, chimerical fusions of both, even as inanimate objects or imitations of werewolves. They are among the most diverse spirits in form, with only the glow of the moon held in common - and even then, not always strongly.'<br /> <br /> It's part of why the Predator's book and Book of Spirits are so good, they do give you some examples and suggestions, but don't limit you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:59:53-08:00","id":825946,"title":"","content":"I think there's another picture of a Lune in Lore of the Forsaken, in the bit discussing Luna. That one looks like a sparkly, moon-themed woman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T08:14:34-08:00","id":825999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824222-how-do-lunes-look?p=825946#post825946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's another picture of a Lune in Lore of the Forsaken, in the bit discussing Luna. That one looks like a sparkly, moon-themed woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be that it was that picture that made some kind of subconscious imprint on me that as model for all the Lunes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:02:42-08:00","id":826401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824222-how-do-lunes-look?p=825999#post825999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could be that it was that picture that made some kind of subconscious imprint on me that as model for all the Lunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it was one of Luna's Masks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T18:03:22-08:00","id":826430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824222-how-do-lunes-look?p=825370#post825370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? That's all you got?<br /> <br /> You should up your special effects budget there, buddy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>BEWARE, FOR THE PATH YOU WILL TAKE WILL LEAD YOU TO CERTAIN DESTRUCTION!<br /> <br /> Thank you, I'll be here all week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T19:49:52-08:00","id":826489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824222-how-do-lunes-look?p=826401#post826401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or it was one of Luna's Masks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could absolutely be, for there are some really nice, in my opinion, depictionsof Mother Luna in different artworks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:49:27-08:00","id":830642,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Here's one example of what a Lune looks like in its lair at a giant theater:</span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The stage itself dominates the far wall, under an archway of ornate gold and ruby, emerald and diamond that would make even the most devout medieval Czar weep. A ragged, blood-red curtain is pulled back under a floor of polished obsidian to reveal the Cahalunim. It is from here where the music emanates, a wall of giant speakers and woofers stacked behind it like a Stonehenge semicircle, amplifying the song. </span></span></span><br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Lune appears to you as a giant coruscating silver star that radiates gloriously, floating and warping subtly to the beat as if it were made from mercurial flame. The heart of an ancient, futuristic reactor born from an artist\u2019s wildest dreamings. It\u2019s bright enough that you have to shield your eyes at first and even then as your pupils constrict painfully not look directly at it.</span></span></span><br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Pure, unadulterated glory.</span></span></span><br /> </div> \u200bAnd (because Lunes change forms):<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As you pull yourself up and over the obsidian lip of the stage, you find that the Lune has changed again, this time far smaller, but no less glorious. You rise to stand before an incarnation that is nearly ten feet tall and made wholly of silvery instrument chords and strings, wrapped and glistening, this wire frame body that vaguely resembles hooded robes, thrumming with sonic vibration. That same Crescent Moon halo glows bright behind its head. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:DarkSlateGray\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Bastian rolls Resolve+Composure: 1 success.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Lunacy is very strong on the stage. You are able to stand before it, but you feel a wave of dizziness that makes your head swim.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The hood lowers as it addresses you. Its choral voice sounds like plucked harps, rising strings, a cresendo of stirring orchestra.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">&quot;[You have come seeking a boon for what lies ahead, a glorious blessing that we alone can give.]&quot;</span></span></span></div> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:53:50-08:00","id":830646,"title":"","content":"This was another from a game I ran, maybe not the most creative, but it worked for a Ralunim emerging from a pool of molten silver:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">A sense of something enormous approaching filled you, and your companion took a frightened step backward with you, trying to interpose himself between you and the titan that rose from the silver lake, but it was a pointless gesture.<br /> <br /> First came the head of the Dragon, long and graceful, eyes opened wide and bright, illuminating the room even more brightly like a pair of round, perfect stars set in its shifting, liquid head as molten silver flowed away from it. Individual scales gleamed like perfect, hammered mithril upon its body, long, strange tendril-like whiskers flowing from its fanged snout.<br /> <br /> It was big, easily bigger than a whale...Like fifty feet from tail to snout, although something made it seem like this was more of a reflection of something greater, a representation of a concept so powerful that to manifest fully in this realm would be destabilizing. It gazed upon you with its all-knowing, all furious gaze, the lunacy growing so loud in your head it felt like your skull would split.<br /> <br /> With a spring and a snap of massive, argent batlike wings, the great wyvern of platinum flew from the pool to land upon the arch above you, perched there, folding its wings and gazing down upon you with an unknowable, eternal stare, the eyes of something getting close to godhood, something that defied the natural laws of the world.<br /> <br /> It locked eyes with you, pinning you in place, focusing entirely upon you, lowering its long neck and revealing fangs that were literally pure shafts of argent light - touching the flames had been one thing but those were pure destruction, like blades of nuclear obliteration within its mouth.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;[DESTROYER...]&quot; </b>It rumbles, voice like an earthquake, like a threatening tidal wave.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;[RAMAEL-THE-THUNDERER RECOGNIZES YOUR SONG.]&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;[GREAT IS OUR DESPAIR.]&quot;</b></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T21:10:33-08:00","id":830787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824222-how-do-lunes-look?p=830642#post830642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The stage itself dominates the far wall, under an archway of ornate gold and ruby, emerald and diamond that would make even the most devout medieval Czar weep. A ragged, blood-red curtain is pulled back under a floor of polished obsidian to reveal the Cahalunim. It is from here where the music emanates, a wall of giant speakers and woofers stacked behind it like a Stonehenge semicircle, amplifying the song. </span></span></span><br /> [/INDENT]<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Lune appears to you as a giant coruscating silver star that radiates gloriously, floating and warping subtly to the beat as if it were made from mercurial flame. The heart of an ancient, futuristic reactor born from an artist\u2019s wildest dreamings. It\u2019s bright enough that you have to shield your eyes at first and even then as your pupils constrict painfully not look directly at it.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this - sounds very much like Lune version of &quot;King in Yellow&quot;. And I love King in Yellow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}